{
  "case_id": "2018-17-1606",
  "document_hash": "3b8170245086fc9eaea9e37f16a125b58aa335ebb3246bca6d6ebcdce0afa1e0",
  "records": [
    {
      "attribution": "Petitioner",
      "case_id": "2018-17-1606",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "3b8170245086fc9eaea9e37f16a125b58aa335ebb3246bca6d6ebcdce0afa1e0",
      "evidence_id": "ev-3b8170245086-0000-0000",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 5,
        "start": 5
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The Appeals Council's decision in this case dismissing Petitioner's request for review as untimely was a final decision on his request for benefits. It brought the administrative review process to a close. After the Appeals Council's decision, there was nothing left for the agency to do, and the agency's denial of benefits became conclusive and binding."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Ginsburg",
      "case_id": "2018-17-1606",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "3b8170245086fc9eaea9e37f16a125b58aa335ebb3246bca6d6ebcdce0afa1e0",
      "evidence_id": "ev-3b8170245086-0000-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 6,
        "start": 6
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE GINSBURG: What about \"after a hearing\"? Those words also, \"final decision after a hearing\"? There's no -- as I understand it, there are never hearings before the Appeals Council."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Petitioner",
      "case_id": "2018-17-1606",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "3b8170245086fc9eaea9e37f16a125b58aa335ebb3246bca6d6ebcdce0afa1e0",
      "evidence_id": "ev-3b8170245086-0000-0003",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 8,
        "start": 8
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "I think what Congress was attempting to do with 405(h) was make clear that the sole avenue for review of final decisions by the Commissioner of Social Security is a complaint filed under Section 405(g)."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "United States",
      "case_id": "2018-17-1606",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "3b8170245086fc9eaea9e37f16a125b58aa335ebb3246bca6d6ebcdce0afa1e0",
      "evidence_id": "ev-3b8170245086-0000-0001",
      "kind": "amicus_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 17,
        "start": 17
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The Social Security Appeals Council dismissal order in this case was a final decision because it marked the agency's last word on Petitioner's application for disability."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "United States",
      "case_id": "2018-17-1606",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "3b8170245086fc9eaea9e37f16a125b58aa335ebb3246bca6d6ebcdce0afa1e0",
      "evidence_id": "ev-3b8170245086-0000-0004",
      "kind": "amicus_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 20,
        "start": 20
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "the existing regulation is a reasonable one. We submit that the answer to that question is no, again, because the plain text of the statute under the plain meaning of final, it -- the agency's decision was conclusive, the agency has no more work to do, and the agency held a hearing in an -- before an administrative law judge on Petitioner's application for Social Security benefits."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Huston",
      "case_id": "2018-17-1606",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "3b8170245086fc9eaea9e37f16a125b58aa335ebb3246bca6d6ebcdce0afa1e0",
      "evidence_id": "ev-3b8170245086-0001-0000",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 24,
        "start": 24
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "I think that's the -- the essential feature of the claimant's claim in this case, that the agency made a mistake in applying its timeliness regulation."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Gupta",
      "case_id": "2018-17-1606",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "document_hash": "3b8170245086fc9eaea9e37f16a125b58aa335ebb3246bca6d6ebcdce0afa1e0",
      "evidence_id": "ev-3b8170245086-0001-0003",
      "kind": "fact",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 26,
        "start": 26
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "There are approximately 22,000 every year, are never reviewable."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Gupta",
      "case_id": "2018-17-1606",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "3b8170245086fc9eaea9e37f16a125b58aa335ebb3246bca6d6ebcdce0afa1e0",
      "evidence_id": "ev-3b8170245086-0001-0004",
      "kind": "stated_consequence",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 30,
        "start": 30
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "the only appropriate remedy is a remand."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Deepak Gupta",
      "case_id": "2018-17-1606",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "3b8170245086fc9eaea9e37f16a125b58aa335ebb3246bca6d6ebcdce0afa1e0",
      "evidence_id": "ev-3b8170245086-0001-0001",
      "kind": "amicus_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 33,
        "start": 33
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The way that Section 405(g) has successfully cabined judicial review for eight decades for the more than a dozen massive claims processes to which it now applies is to limit judicial review not just to any final agency action but to a particular kind of action."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice GORSUCH",
      "case_id": "2018-17-1606",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "3b8170245086fc9eaea9e37f16a125b58aa335ebb3246bca6d6ebcdce0afa1e0",
      "evidence_id": "ev-3b8170245086-0002-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 45,
        "start": 45
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "You'd agree that -- that the Social Security Administration could grant a hearing that it is not statutorily compelled to give?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2018-17-1606",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "3b8170245086fc9eaea9e37f16a125b58aa335ebb3246bca6d6ebcdce0afa1e0",
      "evidence_id": "ev-3b8170245086-0002-0001",
      "kind": "procedural_event",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 46,
        "start": 46
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "There was a hearing on -- on the question of benefits."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. GUpta",
      "case_id": "2018-17-1606",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "3b8170245086fc9eaea9e37f16a125b58aa335ebb3246bca6d6ebcdce0afa1e0",
      "evidence_id": "ev-3b8170245086-0002-0002",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 49,
        "start": 49
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Congress was not concerned -- Congress's concern was with ensuring that this entire massive process was governed by law. It was not directing cases into the federal courts for error correction purposes. It was doing so to ensure that -- that there would be a judicial oversight of the process and that when people had exhausted completely through the process and had a determination on the merits, that that merits determination on eligibility or amount would be reviewed in court."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice BREYER",
      "case_id": "2018-17-1606",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "3b8170245086fc9eaea9e37f16a125b58aa335ebb3246bca6d6ebcdce0afa1e0",
      "evidence_id": "ev-3b8170245086-0002-0003",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 51,
        "start": 51
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "But what does the link is the word \"after\"."
    },
    {
